- decided_at: '2026-09-08T00:35:00+00:00'
  event: initial
  value: Pursue the converse (Fano plus single-letterization) and treat achievability as a separate project that is not funded until the operational scenario is settled.
  reason: The converse is an impossibility result - no scheme recovers more than log(5/4) nats per use about the route - which is the shape of claim the paper actually makes. Achievability would restate a classical Z-channel result at high formalization cost and sits awkwardly against the paper's thesis. Achievability also presupposes that someone chooses route sequences to encode messages, which is an interpretive claim about context lifting that has not been established.
